WEBVTT

00:00:17.760 --> 00:00:20.060
Wait, is that Fujiko?

00:00:20.470 --> 00:00:21.640
Hey!

00:00:22.230 --> 00:00:25.980
Is that really you over there, Fujiko?

00:00:26.560 --> 00:00:27.770
Yes, it's me!

00:00:28.110 --> 00:00:29.940
Is that you, Hana? Where are you?

00:00:31.940 --> 00:00:33.570
I'm coming your way now!

00:00:33.650 --> 00:00:35.450
I want you guys to stay put.

00:00:35.860 --> 00:00:38.950
It's dangerous to follow me down.
Just wait here.

00:00:44.250 --> 00:00:45.460
<i>They're alive.</i>

00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:47.080
<i>They're still alive!</i>

00:00:48.040 --> 00:00:52.880
<i>Fujiko, I know you might be upset with me
for going off on my own.</i>

00:00:53.260 --> 00:00:55.300
<i>You might even be sick of me.</i>

00:00:56.630 --> 00:00:57.510
<i>But even so...</i>

00:01:00.010 --> 00:01:01.220
Hana...

00:01:01.390 --> 00:01:02.310
It's Hana.

00:01:04.850 --> 00:01:06.100
You're alive.

00:02:46.490 --> 00:02:47.950
RAIN WATER

00:02:48.040 --> 00:02:50.120
<i>Jeez, your hair is a frizzy mess.</i>

00:02:50.210 --> 00:02:52.500
You look like you were raised in a barn.

00:02:54.250 --> 00:02:57.170
It's funny since you used to look like
such a princess.

00:02:57.260 --> 00:02:59.510
You're one to talk, Chisa.

00:02:59.590 --> 00:03:01.510
You're the closest one to a princess here.

00:03:02.430 --> 00:03:06.680
I won't lie, Hana. I was totally ready
to punch you if we ever met again.

00:03:06.890 --> 00:03:08.140
Tell us what happened.

00:03:09.980 --> 00:03:14.400
My skin got covered in this weird,
gooey, purple stuff.

00:03:15.020 --> 00:03:16.400
<i>It just kept spreading.</i>

00:03:16.480 --> 00:03:19.990
<i>Mr. Aramaki told me that it dissolves
living things into piles of goop.</i>

00:03:20.950 --> 00:03:22.360
I thought I was going to die.

00:03:23.110 --> 00:03:25.370
I didn't want anybody to have to see it.

00:03:25.870 --> 00:03:28.080
I knew it. So that's why you left.

00:03:28.660 --> 00:03:31.370
But honestly,
you should have just told us about it.

00:03:31.540 --> 00:03:34.920
In the end, we were all really sad
and worried sick about you.

00:03:36.500 --> 00:03:37.500
Sorry.

00:03:38.630 --> 00:03:43.720
Okay, then. Let's catch up with each other
over some dinner.

00:03:44.930 --> 00:03:46.430
Please cook something up.

00:03:47.930 --> 00:03:48.970
My pleasure.

00:03:49.060 --> 00:03:50.600
Come this way, Hana.

00:03:50.680 --> 00:03:52.440
Fujiko seems so happy now.

00:03:53.310 --> 00:03:55.440
She's been depressed this whole time.

00:03:56.360 --> 00:03:58.690
All we did is look for food every day

00:03:59.280 --> 00:04:02.110
while our bodies grew weaker
and we lost hope.

00:04:02.610 --> 00:04:06.240
<i>Now that she mentioned it,
they look thinner than before.</i>

00:04:06.320 --> 00:04:07.410
Above all else,

00:04:07.780 --> 00:04:09.950
the hardest thing was
dealing with the thought

00:04:10.040 --> 00:04:11.790
that we might never see anybody again.

00:04:12.580 --> 00:04:15.170
That's why
I'm also happy we found someone.

00:04:15.920 --> 00:04:17.340
Especially since it was you, Hana.

00:04:17.920 --> 00:04:19.090
It's given me strength.

00:04:20.920 --> 00:04:24.840
Then the area got hit by a flood
and everything was ruined.

00:04:24.930 --> 00:04:29.310
Because of the change in terrain,
we couldn't go back to where we came from.

00:04:29.850 --> 00:04:34.810
Luckily, we were already carrying
some supplies, so we traveled around.

00:04:35.600 --> 00:04:37.650
And after some time, we settled down here.

00:04:37.730 --> 00:04:42.900
Mr. Aramaki and Haru came after me,
so we traveled west together.

00:04:43.610 --> 00:04:46.860
Then we found one of the shelters
and met Team Autumn inside.

00:04:46.950 --> 00:04:49.700
Really? You met another team?

00:04:49.780 --> 00:04:50.700
Yes.

00:04:50.990 --> 00:04:54.790
After that, we ended up traveling
with Team Autumn for a while.

00:04:55.210 --> 00:04:57.290
Oh, Momota is doing fine, by the way.

00:04:57.380 --> 00:05:00.250
Is that so? Great! So you found him?

00:05:00.340 --> 00:05:03.590
Yes, he was picked up by Team Summer A...

00:05:11.560 --> 00:05:12.890
<i>It all came back to me just now.</i>

00:05:13.390 --> 00:05:15.350
<i>I was almost killed by those two.</i>

00:05:17.650 --> 00:05:21.940
Hey, guys, wasn't that a missile
that just passed us?

00:05:22.030 --> 00:05:23.570
Are you crazy?

00:05:23.650 --> 00:05:26.820
There's no way those are missiles.
They're probably fuel or something.

00:05:26.900 --> 00:05:28.410
Right, Ryo?

00:05:29.990 --> 00:05:34.370
Well, we can't fill our stomachs
with missiles, so it doesn't even matter.

00:05:34.450 --> 00:05:35.830
For sure.

00:05:35.910 --> 00:05:38.540
Anyways,
I really wonder where Nat went off to.

00:05:38.620 --> 00:05:42.000
More importantly, we need to go up,
but there's no way to get there.

00:05:42.090 --> 00:05:44.260
Which means we only have one choice.

00:05:45.420 --> 00:05:47.630
-Semmy!
-Here goes nothing!

00:05:51.640 --> 00:05:52.680
Hey!

00:05:56.680 --> 00:05:58.310
Sorry!

00:05:58.520 --> 00:06:01.440
Was I being too cocky again?
I got caught up in the moment.

00:06:02.320 --> 00:06:03.230
Whatever.

00:06:03.610 --> 00:06:06.900
Live like the idiot you are.
That's the best way to handle it.

00:06:07.860 --> 00:06:09.490
Let's get over there too, Matsuri.

00:06:17.370 --> 00:06:19.790
You've gotten the gist of it, Natsu.

00:06:20.040 --> 00:06:21.500
Just don't overextend your body.

00:06:26.010 --> 00:06:27.170
There's water leaking.

00:06:27.800 --> 00:06:29.470
Be careful not to slip down there!

00:06:33.260 --> 00:06:36.100
Natsu! Use your left hand
to grab onto that pipe!

00:06:38.100 --> 00:06:42.190
<i>Good. Don't fall again. Never again!</i>

00:06:45.110 --> 00:06:46.230
Natsu!

00:06:51.610 --> 00:06:54.780
Are you okay, Natsu? Did you get hurt?

00:06:55.990 --> 00:06:59.370
I bumped my knee a little,
but I'm all right.

00:06:59.830 --> 00:07:02.380
Hey, Ango! Natsu is just fine!

00:07:02.960 --> 00:07:05.340
It's all thanks to you
keeping hold of her rope!

00:07:07.550 --> 00:07:08.460
Ango?

00:07:18.640 --> 00:07:21.690
Hey, Ango? Is something the matter?

00:07:22.310 --> 00:07:23.310
Ango?

00:07:24.270 --> 00:07:25.480
You idiots.

00:07:25.570 --> 00:07:29.030
If you climb up here like that,
then the rope is meaningless.

00:07:30.740 --> 00:07:31.700
Ango?

00:07:32.990 --> 00:07:35.200
He fell... straight down...

00:07:35.870 --> 00:07:37.080
Shigeru...

00:07:37.700 --> 00:07:38.950
Shigeru!

00:07:39.700 --> 00:07:41.790
Ryo cut the rope.

00:07:42.120 --> 00:07:45.170
But it was all my fault.

00:07:45.790 --> 00:07:47.040
I'm the one who killed him!

00:07:47.670 --> 00:07:49.050
Who is Shigeru?

00:07:49.130 --> 00:07:52.220
You climbed
a limestone cave before, right?

00:07:52.800 --> 00:07:54.340
With this Shigeru person.

00:07:54.590 --> 00:07:55.930
What happened back then?

00:07:57.430 --> 00:07:58.810
It was a test.

00:07:59.640 --> 00:08:02.020
A test designed to choose seven of us.

00:08:02.850 --> 00:08:05.860
But Shigeru failed! And Nobara! And Mayu!

00:08:06.060 --> 00:08:07.730
They're all gone!

00:08:08.230 --> 00:08:10.990
They were killed!
Everyone except the seven of us!

00:08:12.030 --> 00:08:14.320
What are you talking about? What test?

00:08:14.410 --> 00:08:15.910
The test!

00:08:16.120 --> 00:08:18.660
The one we risked our lives on
to decide the seven

00:08:18.740 --> 00:08:20.450
who would go to the future!

00:08:27.920 --> 00:08:30.050
Did you just hear a voice?

00:08:30.130 --> 00:08:31.260
No.

00:08:31.340 --> 00:08:33.220
All I hear is the noise of the machines.

00:08:44.310 --> 00:08:46.940
-A test designed to choose seven of us.
-It's coming from here.

00:08:47.230 --> 00:08:49.270
What? Doesn't that sound like Ango?

00:08:49.360 --> 00:08:50.730
It totally sounds like Ango.

00:08:50.820 --> 00:08:52.110
The test!

00:08:52.320 --> 00:08:54.740
The one we risked our lives on
to decide the seven

00:08:54.860 --> 00:08:56.780
who would go to the future!

00:08:57.370 --> 00:08:58.530
<i>That idiot.</i>

00:08:58.950 --> 00:09:00.790
<i>There he goes
shooting his mouth off again.</i>

00:09:00.870 --> 00:09:02.700
Are you serious?

00:09:03.370 --> 00:09:05.040
They really did something like that?

00:09:05.580 --> 00:09:07.290
Just for the 7SEEDS Project?

00:09:07.380 --> 00:09:09.210
All the members of Summer A...

00:09:09.670 --> 00:09:11.250
That's how they were chosen?

00:09:11.340 --> 00:09:12.840
That's so cruel!

00:09:12.920 --> 00:09:15.010
You'll never know what it was like.

00:09:15.840 --> 00:09:17.970
You got to come here for nothing.

00:09:18.050 --> 00:09:21.310
You're right.
I can't even begin to imagine.

00:09:21.760 --> 00:09:22.810
That's just too cruel.

00:09:22.890 --> 00:09:24.270
You have no idea!

00:09:25.520 --> 00:09:29.610
That test was made
just to select the seven of us.

00:09:30.020 --> 00:09:31.770
It was all we lived for...

00:09:33.110 --> 00:09:34.280
Nothing else...

00:09:34.360 --> 00:09:36.900
Yes, I can't understand it at all.

00:09:37.360 --> 00:09:41.240
But why didn't you try to run away
from something so terrible?

00:09:45.080 --> 00:09:46.210
Run away?

00:09:47.540 --> 00:09:50.170
-That's Arashi!
-Hooray! That's definitely Arashi's voice!

00:09:50.250 --> 00:09:51.590
Hey! Ara--

00:09:52.590 --> 00:09:53.630
"Run away"?

00:09:57.510 --> 00:10:01.680
Yes, couldn't you have worked together
to revolt and tie up the professors,

00:10:02.050 --> 00:10:05.430
then run away and get help somehow?

00:10:06.930 --> 00:10:09.730
Were you trapped on an island
or in a prison somewhere?

00:10:10.310 --> 00:10:12.770
Or were you held hostage by armed men?

00:10:12.860 --> 00:10:14.860
No, it was nothing like that.

00:10:15.650 --> 00:10:17.570
We were just in the wilderness somewhere.

00:10:19.030 --> 00:10:20.820
What do you mean by "run away"?

00:10:20.950 --> 00:10:23.700
If we ran away, we would lose
our chance to be one of the chosen!

00:10:23.780 --> 00:10:24.830
What?

00:10:25.370 --> 00:10:27.250
Then are you saying
that you agreed to be there?

00:10:27.660 --> 00:10:30.040
You willingly took that test
because you wanted to?

00:10:30.290 --> 00:10:32.880
No... but I...

00:10:33.170 --> 00:10:35.920
Then did you do it
because you desired to go to the future?

00:10:37.470 --> 00:10:40.010
That's right! I wanted to go!

00:10:40.220 --> 00:10:43.010
I wanted to be one of the chosen seven
no matter what!

00:10:43.100 --> 00:10:44.470
Isn't that obvious?

00:10:44.560 --> 00:10:47.980
Then you're proud to have succeeded?

00:10:48.930 --> 00:10:50.100
No.

00:10:50.190 --> 00:10:52.190
Ango, what's the matter with you?

00:10:52.270 --> 00:10:53.860
What you're saying is crazy!

00:10:54.020 --> 00:10:57.320
You're in so much pain right now,
there's nothing "obvious" about this.

00:10:57.900 --> 00:11:01.160
What did those professors
do to all of you?

00:11:03.570 --> 00:11:04.990
Hey, Ryo.

00:11:05.490 --> 00:11:08.250
Were you also part of all this stuff?

00:11:09.040 --> 00:11:12.710
Let's get this off and pass through here.
They must be at the other end.

00:11:12.960 --> 00:11:14.090
Okay, sure.

00:11:14.170 --> 00:11:16.920
Did you all take that test
knowing what would happen?

00:11:17.510 --> 00:11:20.880
You were all fine with your friends dying,
so long as you got to go to the future?

00:11:21.800 --> 00:11:23.720
Is that seriously how you felt about it?

00:11:25.810 --> 00:11:28.560
If that's true,
then you were essentially brainwashed!

00:11:30.560 --> 00:11:34.270
Why can't Mayu be the one to go?
Why did I have to be chosen? Why?

00:11:37.860 --> 00:11:39.490
What do you mean "brainwashed"?

00:11:39.570 --> 00:11:42.110
Arashi, are you calling us stupid?

00:11:42.200 --> 00:11:43.700
It wasn't what you wanted.

00:11:44.160 --> 00:11:46.990
It wasn't your idea.
It was the professors' wishes.

00:11:47.080 --> 00:11:49.660
I did think about it!
I thought about it a lot!

00:11:49.750 --> 00:11:51.960
I spent every damn day
wracking my brains out!

00:11:52.040 --> 00:11:53.750
How to pass my classes!

00:11:54.330 --> 00:11:57.000
How to take the top spot!
How to avoid dropping out!

00:11:57.710 --> 00:11:59.630
I thought about it all on my own!

00:11:59.710 --> 00:12:03.430
How to pass the final test
and become one of the final seven!

00:12:04.390 --> 00:12:06.930
Did you think about
why you were taking the test?

00:12:08.600 --> 00:12:11.600
About what motivated
you to go to the future?

00:12:13.520 --> 00:12:17.110
About why you never considered
running away?

00:12:18.190 --> 00:12:21.280
About what it is
that's making your body quiver right now?

00:12:27.240 --> 00:12:29.120
<i>Why did I study?</i>

00:12:29.990 --> 00:12:31.290
<i>Why did I aim to be the top?</i>

00:12:31.910 --> 00:12:33.120
<i>Why did I take the test?</i>

00:12:34.960 --> 00:12:38.920
<i>Why can't I come up with an answer?
I should know already.</i>

00:12:39.460 --> 00:12:40.840
I'm sorry.

00:12:41.260 --> 00:12:44.720
Asking why you didn't run away
was a horrible thing for me to do.

00:12:45.760 --> 00:12:48.680
But it really pisses me off,
what those professors did to you!

00:12:49.930 --> 00:12:55.600
What makes me even angrier than
the fact that they killed so many

00:12:56.100 --> 00:12:59.190
is that they brainwashed all of you
to be unable to think for yourselves!

00:12:59.940 --> 00:13:02.820
Those professors stole your ability
to think freely, Ango!

00:13:05.400 --> 00:13:07.950
<i>Living in a world where running away
isn't an option?</i>

00:13:08.530 --> 00:13:11.370
<i>I can't imagine
the horror you faced, Ango.</i>

00:13:11.450 --> 00:13:14.000
A world without a place
to escape to is just wrong.

00:13:14.660 --> 00:13:18.420
The ability to make the choice
to flee and protect yourself

00:13:18.920 --> 00:13:20.130
is an absolute necessity!

00:13:21.130 --> 00:13:26.300
To me, it's like you were ordered
to mindlessly fight for your country!

00:13:26.800 --> 00:13:29.720
You were all just strung along
by the will of some other person.

00:13:31.510 --> 00:13:33.640
I hate that more than anything.

00:13:34.890 --> 00:13:36.600
And it's still mostly true even now.

00:13:36.690 --> 00:13:38.100
You're wrong, Arashi!

00:13:38.190 --> 00:13:39.770
For us, there was never an option to--

00:13:39.860 --> 00:13:40.900
There was!

00:13:41.480 --> 00:13:42.780
You had that option,

00:13:43.570 --> 00:13:45.320
but you were made to never realize it!

00:13:46.150 --> 00:13:48.240
You were manipulated into thinking
you had no choice!

00:13:48.320 --> 00:13:49.620
Even in the face of death!

00:13:49.700 --> 00:13:51.030
No, Arashi! You're wrong!

00:13:51.120 --> 00:13:53.160
They wanted you to think
you made that choice!

00:13:53.240 --> 00:13:54.250
Arashi, stop it!

00:13:54.330 --> 00:13:55.540
Listen, Ango!

00:13:55.620 --> 00:13:58.790
You didn't have to take that test!

00:14:11.550 --> 00:14:13.600
It was the same for our team.

00:14:14.600 --> 00:14:19.270
We were never asked what we wanted,
or given a choice or a chance to refuse.

00:14:19.940 --> 00:14:24.190
We were thrown into it by someone else
without even being able to say goodbye.

00:14:24.280 --> 00:14:29.320
You were brainwashed into wanting to go
and put here according to someone's plan.

00:14:30.110 --> 00:14:32.240
We're all the same, Ango.

00:14:32.780 --> 00:14:34.540
Team Summer A and B.

00:14:35.580 --> 00:14:38.330
But now it's different. We're free.

00:14:39.420 --> 00:14:41.580
We can choose to do
what we want by ourselves.

00:14:42.840 --> 00:14:43.840
That includes you, Ango.

00:14:47.590 --> 00:14:49.010
We were manipulated?

00:14:50.970 --> 00:14:52.470
We didn't have to take the test?

00:14:54.050 --> 00:14:57.430
But then,
that just makes us all seem like idiots.

00:14:58.810 --> 00:15:03.150
That means Shigeru died taking a test
he never needed to take?

00:15:07.690 --> 00:15:09.030
Shigeru...

00:15:09.320 --> 00:15:11.450
He died because of me instead...

00:15:11.530 --> 00:15:12.740
Ango, listen!

00:15:12.820 --> 00:15:16.040
Whatever happened back then,
you're not responsible for any of it!

00:15:19.160 --> 00:15:20.250
<i>Just think...</i>

00:15:20.620 --> 00:15:21.710
<i>on our own?</i>

00:15:22.500 --> 00:15:23.500
Ango.

00:15:28.840 --> 00:15:29.840
Ryo?

00:15:29.970 --> 00:15:32.090
Semimaru and Matsuri are with him too.

00:15:32.180 --> 00:15:34.050
Hi, Nat!

00:15:34.140 --> 00:15:35.720
Hey, Arashi!

00:15:35.800 --> 00:15:37.770
Where the hell did you go off to?

00:15:37.850 --> 00:15:39.430
We were really worried about you, man!

00:15:39.520 --> 00:15:40.640
Ryo...

00:15:41.230 --> 00:15:44.860
Ango, there's something important
that I haven't told you.

00:15:46.020 --> 00:15:49.860
I wasn't able to decide
whether I should tell you or not.

00:15:50.400 --> 00:15:53.740
At the time,
I thought it was better not to tell you.

00:15:54.320 --> 00:15:56.240
But that was probably a mistake.

00:15:57.200 --> 00:15:58.290
I should have told you.

00:15:58.990 --> 00:16:01.040
What... was it?

00:16:01.620 --> 00:16:04.040
During the test, in the cave,

00:16:04.630 --> 00:16:08.630
<i>when you and Shigeru were suspended,
the one who actually cut the rope...</i>

00:16:09.340 --> 00:16:10.510
<i>was Shigeru.</i>

00:16:11.470 --> 00:16:14.800
Where is this coming from?
We both know you cut it.

00:16:14.890 --> 00:16:18.260
Yes, I did.
We did it at nearly the same time.

00:16:18.930 --> 00:16:23.440
But I could feel the moment that he cut
the rope because it was in my hand.

00:16:24.770 --> 00:16:28.440
Shigeru cut it himself
in order to save you.

00:16:28.520 --> 00:16:29.690
Quit lying.

00:16:30.190 --> 00:16:31.610
Shigeru wasn't--

00:16:31.690 --> 00:16:33.030
You think he wasn't capable.

00:16:33.700 --> 00:16:35.320
I know what you think of him.

00:16:36.320 --> 00:16:37.950
Frankly, I thought the same thing.

00:16:38.990 --> 00:16:41.410
He was always so slow and indecisive.

00:16:42.250 --> 00:16:45.960
<i>He would rely on you constantly
and couldn't do anything without you.</i>

00:16:46.380 --> 00:16:48.210
<i>He was a worthless weakling.</i>

00:16:48.290 --> 00:16:50.710
-I never thought--
-But you did!

00:16:51.800 --> 00:16:53.920
You thought it was impossible
for him to ever save you.

00:16:54.510 --> 00:16:56.090
You would never allow it to happen.

00:16:57.850 --> 00:17:00.470
Out of everyone,
you acknowledged his abilities the least.

00:17:01.890 --> 00:17:06.190
I was watching Shigeru that day,
before I even went into the cave.

00:17:06.690 --> 00:17:09.730
<i>Ukai was out to kill you
and Shigeru fought back against him.</i>

00:17:10.150 --> 00:17:14.950
<i>Shigeru got shot and endured the pain
to descend into the cave to save you.</i>

00:17:15.900 --> 00:17:17.570
Don't tell Ango about this, okay?

00:17:18.620 --> 00:17:20.950
If you do, he'll only start worrying
about me again.

00:17:22.200 --> 00:17:25.870
For once, I get to be the one
who worries and looks after Ango.

00:17:26.960 --> 00:17:28.460
It's a rare chance for me.

00:17:28.960 --> 00:17:30.710
I saw him in a new light.

00:17:31.420 --> 00:17:35.380
He proved himself far more useful
than you were that evening.

00:17:37.380 --> 00:17:40.470
I know you won't admit
that he was skillful and brave.

00:17:41.310 --> 00:17:45.680
You want to believe that Shigeru died
because of your actions, right?

00:17:46.600 --> 00:17:49.940
Apparently,
that feeling is called "egoism."

00:17:52.780 --> 00:17:55.900
Ango, it's time for you
to appreciate him already.

00:17:56.780 --> 00:18:00.780
Shigeru fought his own fights
and called his own shots.

00:18:01.120 --> 00:18:04.910
<i>He went into the cave on his own
and took the lead when climbing out.</i>

00:18:05.000 --> 00:18:07.830
He caused his own injuries
and made his own mistakes,

00:18:08.290 --> 00:18:10.330
and ultimately cut the rope
of his own accord.

00:18:11.340 --> 00:18:14.000
He took responsibility
and made that decision for himself.

00:18:14.510 --> 00:18:17.090
He did everything he could,
despite his mistakes!

00:18:17.670 --> 00:18:18.590
Do you get it?

00:18:18.680 --> 00:18:20.970
You had absolutely nothing
to do with his death!

00:18:21.510 --> 00:18:24.600
He caused his own death
because he wanted to save you.

00:18:26.270 --> 00:18:30.020
And to him,
that must have been a source of pride.

00:18:32.940 --> 00:18:33.940
Just admit it.

00:18:34.610 --> 00:18:36.860
Shigeru wasn't someone
you had to take care of.

00:18:37.440 --> 00:18:40.660
He's not some supporting character
in your life story.

00:18:41.240 --> 00:18:44.240
For God's sake,
admit that he was his own man!

00:18:45.790 --> 00:18:49.410
Ango, I'm going to save you
no matter what. Okay?

00:18:56.420 --> 00:18:59.050
Shigeru told Ukai,

00:19:00.130 --> 00:19:02.260
"Ango has to go to the future.

00:19:03.260 --> 00:19:06.010
He took action and owned up
to the consequences.

00:19:06.560 --> 00:19:09.390
That's the kind of person
who has to go to the future."

00:19:09.980 --> 00:19:10.940
I heard it all.

00:19:12.060 --> 00:19:12.900
Enough, Ango.

00:19:13.940 --> 00:19:16.150
Now's the time to be that person!

00:19:21.910 --> 00:19:22.870
Ango.

00:19:24.200 --> 00:19:26.620
You never really trusted me, did you?

00:19:27.740 --> 00:19:30.080
I was just like a pet or a lackey to you.

00:19:31.000 --> 00:19:33.790
I've always wanted us to be friends
who stood on equal ground.

00:19:34.380 --> 00:19:35.790
We are friends.

00:19:35.880 --> 00:19:40.800
Okay, then you won't get upset
if I get better scores than you, right?

00:19:41.430 --> 00:19:43.680
No, I will.

00:19:44.470 --> 00:19:46.510
Because that means
we would become rivals, right?

00:19:47.970 --> 00:19:50.310
I think "rival" has a nice ring to it.

00:19:52.560 --> 00:19:56.060
Shigeru, there's something
I never got a chance to say to you.

00:19:56.900 --> 00:19:58.070
Really? What's that?

00:19:59.280 --> 00:20:01.820
I never said it
because I was too stubborn.

00:20:07.410 --> 00:20:11.250
If you hadn't come for me then,
I would have died for sure.

00:20:12.660 --> 00:20:15.130
Thank you for coming to save my life.

00:20:16.130 --> 00:20:17.170
And also...

00:20:18.300 --> 00:20:19.920
I'm sorry for everything.

00:20:24.380 --> 00:20:26.550
Do your best in the future, Ango.

00:20:30.810 --> 00:20:31.810
See you later.

00:21:05.550 --> 00:21:06.720
Time to go.

00:21:07.260 --> 00:21:09.550
We'll all climb up
and then regroup at the top.

00:21:12.100 --> 00:21:14.730
Ango, are you up for it?

00:21:15.520 --> 00:21:16.650
Arashi.

00:21:33.290 --> 00:21:35.540
You, sheltered kids, can't compare.

00:21:36.210 --> 00:21:37.920
Sheltered, right?

00:21:38.210 --> 00:21:39.580
I get it now.

00:21:40.130 --> 00:21:42.630
Hey, man, that's why I told you before,

00:21:42.710 --> 00:21:44.760
being sheltered isn't a bad thing.

00:21:45.340 --> 00:21:49.010
Outcasts who grow up in the wild
can never be sophisticated.

00:21:49.390 --> 00:21:53.600
But sophisticated people can
act like outcasts if they want to.

00:21:53.680 --> 00:21:55.180
You have a way with words.

00:21:55.270 --> 00:21:57.690
I know, right?
Keep that praise coming, Ryo!

00:22:01.690 --> 00:22:04.070
Natsu, do your best to climb up.

00:22:04.150 --> 00:22:05.150
Climb up on your own.

00:22:05.240 --> 00:22:06.450
Right!

00:22:11.740 --> 00:22:15.200
<i>But now it's different. We're free.</i>

00:22:16.790 --> 00:22:18.790
<i>We can choose to do
what we want by ourselves.</i>
